\begin{abstract}
We develop explicit and fully rigorous formulas for a concrete admissible Gaussian family in the Weil quadratic-form framework. We prove an exact shifted-Gaussian autocorrelation decomposition that includes both cosine and sine modulations, a quantitative exponential decoupling bound with an explicit constant, and a complex-frequency amplification identity with explicit relative error control. We also establish exact mass and $L^2$ identities, a spectral curvature formula at the origin, a large-frequency asymptotic, a parameter-sensitivity identity, a phase-discriminant lemma, and a local finite-part regularization formula near a zero of the Riemann zeta function. Using the standard Guinand--Weil/Bombieri decomposition, we derive a fully explicit conditional inequality for weighted prime sums under the Riemann Hypothesis. All computations are self-contained and all constants are explicit.
\end{abstract}

