\section{Conclusion}
%=======================================================================

We have given a self-contained treatment of a concrete admissible Gaussian family in the Weil framework.
The principal results are:

\begin{itemize}[nosep]
\item an exact shifted-Gaussian autocorrelation decomposition with both cosine and sine modulations;
\item exact mass, $L^2$, and spectral-curvature identities;
\item a large-frequency asymptotic profile and parameter-sensitivity formulas;
\item an explicit exponential decoupling estimate;
\item a complex-frequency amplification identity with explicit relative error control;
\item a phase-discriminant lemma;
\item a local finite-part regularization formula near a zeta zero;
\item and the standard RH-conditional prime-sum inequality.
\end{itemize}

All formulas are explicit, all proofs are elementary, and the resulting identities are suitable for numerical exploration and for structural work in explicit-formula methods.

